<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brotherhood of Blackheads</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">14th century–<a href="/years/1940">1940</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as House of the Blackheads, Brotherhood of the Blackheads</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Brotherhood of Blackheads was an association of unmarried merchants, ship-owners and foreign traders in the towns of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonia">Livonia</a>, first recorded in Reval (Tallinn) around 1400 and later in Riga. Its members joined in the defence of the town and held festivities in their own house. Its patron was Saint Maurice, shown as a Moor on its arms. It existed until 1940.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/brotherhood-of-blackheads.jpg" alt="Brotherhood of Blackheads" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original uploader was Brunswyk at de.wikipedia (Original text : de:Benutzer:Brunswyk) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tallinn_Schwarzhaupterhaus.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
